  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Dmitry Nagiyev tastes the dish. He takes a bite and is absolutely amazed. We'll hear it in Russian first; don't worry about catching every word.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это божественно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это очень вкусно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я не ожидал такого.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Повезло тебе, поварёнок.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Дмитрий Владимирович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну, всем повезло.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Наш ресторан лучший.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Гости очень довольны.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы сделали это.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Теперь можно отдыхать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отличная работа, команда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Браво!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's go through it line by line. Nagiyev closes his eyes in delight.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это божественно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is divine.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'this' straight to 'divinely'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это очень вкусно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is very tasty.' Notice the word order: 'this' comes first, and 'it's tasty' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я не ожидал такого.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I didn't expect this.' Here 'I' sets up the idea, while 'such' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Повезло тебе, поварёнок.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You're lucky, little chef.' You'll hear 'it was lucky' all the time in the show, here connected with 'little cook'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Дмитрий Владимирович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Dmitry Vladimirovich.' The key word here means 'Dmitry', which Dmitry combines with 'Vladimirovich'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну, всем повезло.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, we're all lucky.' A compact expression built around 'to everyone' and 'it was lucky'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Наш ресторан лучший.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Our restaurant is the best.' Dmitry puts 'restaurant' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'best'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Гости очень довольны.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The guests are very pleased.' In Russian, 'visitors' leads into 'satisfied' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы сделали это.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We did it.' The first content word means 'we', and 'this' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Теперь можно отдыхать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Now we can rest.' The key word here means 'now', which Dmitry combines with 'may'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отличная работа, команда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Excellent work, team.' Listen for the word meaning 'excellent' right alongside 'job' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Браво!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Bravo!' You'll hear 'bravo' all the time in the show, here connected with 'bravo'. Now let's hear the whole scene once more, start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
